# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# Model weights and caches are excluded; RUN RECORDS ARE NOT.
#
# Every number in either paper is derived from result.json, config.json,
# log.csv and grad_log.json, all of which are committed. The checkpoints
# are only needed to re-score an agent without retraining it, and they
# are far too large for a git repository (Phase 2 alone holds 66 runs of
# several MB each). If you need them, retrain: the run directory name
# encodes every setting, and training is deterministic up to the
# threading caveat documented in Paper A Section 6.4.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
*.pt
*.pth
*.ckpt
*.npz
*.npy
*.h5

# dataset caches, rebuilt on demand from the generators in dataset.py.
# Each is a few MB of trajectories keyed by a hash of the generating
# settings; dataset.py regenerates them deterministically, and the hash
# is recorded as `dataset_version` in every result.json so results from
# different trajectory versions can be told apart.
**/data/datasets/
**/data/cache/
**/.dataset_cache/

# timestamped safety copies made by the sweep drivers before overwriting
# anything. Useful locally, noise in a repository.
**/runs_backup_*/
**/runs_old*/
**/*_backup/

# python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/
env/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# latex build products; the .tex and figures/ are committed
*.aux
*.log
*.out
*.toc
*.lof
*.lot
*.fls
*.fdb_latexmk
*.synctex.gz
*.bbl
*.blg
*.nav
*.snm
*.vrb

# os / editor
.DS_Store
._*
# Word lock files, created while a .docx is open
~$*
*.tmp
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
Thumbs.db
*.swp
*~
.idea/
.vscode/

# local run logs: large, machine-specific, and not inputs to any result.
# The per-run log.csv files inside runs/ ARE committed; these are the
# driver-script stdout captures.
logs/
logs_remaining/
logs_ablation/
logs_replication/
nohup.out

# credentials. IONQ_API_KEY is read from the environment and must never
# be written to a file in this tree.
.env
*.key
*_secret*
credentials*
